+# ADR-0017: ERP port operation `readAdvisor` for advisor master data
+
+- **Status:** Proposed
+- **Date:** 2026-11-04
+- **Deciders:** <tech lead>
+- **Sources:** T2-C-010, T2-D-009, T3-D-005, T3-AC-001, [ERP conventions](../conventions/erp.md), [spec](../specs/draft-advisor-master-data/spec.md)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data that the ERP holds (T2-C-010: customer and advisor master data). The ERP port has only `readCustomer`. Every module reaches the ERP only through the `integration` module and its port (T3-D-005, T3-AC-001). A copy records its source and age (T2-D-009); the `integration` module gives each read the same envelope (`ErpRead`: source, source version, read time). T2 section 4 allows synchronous ERP reads only at the checkout, and T3-D-007 fills copies by a schedule or an event, never by a user request. The `identity` module owns the person and reads customer and advisor master data through `integration` (architecture section 4), so this read needs a new port operation, a new payload contract and a first dependency from `identity` on `integration`.
+
+## Options
+
+1. **A separate operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber)` with its own payload `AdvisorMasterData`.** Good: one operation per payload, as the port rules ask; the contract can grow without touching the customer read. Bad: one more method for each adapter.
+2. **Extend `readCustomer` to also return advisors.** Good: one method. Bad: mixes two keys (`K` and `B` numbers) and two payloads in one operation; every caller must branch on the type.
+3. **Read the advisor from a copy in `erp_copy`.** Good: no ERP call per read. Bad: needs a table, a schedule and reconciliation that no current story asks for.
+
+## Decision
+
+We choose option 1. The payload is `AdvisorMasterData { advisorNumber (B + 5 digits), givenName, familyName, email, active, sourceVersion }`. `integration` exposes `readAdvisor(advisorNumber)` as `ErpRead<AdvisorMasterData> | null`. `identity` receives `Integration` as a dependency and exposes `getAdvisor(advisorNumber)`; it does not store the result. A copy (option 3) can follow when a story needs it, behind the same `identity` API.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Each adapter (`erp-fake` now, `erp-nav` and `erp-bc` later) implements `readAdvisor`. The NAV field mapping is open until the contract work (T2 section 3).
+- `identity` depends on the `integration` public API (reads only). `pnpm arch` forbids a cycle, so `integration` cannot depend on `identity`.
+- Every call reaches the ERP. An ERP outage throws `ErpUnavailableError` (re-exported by `integration`) to the caller.
+- A synchronous read outside the checkout departs from T2 section 4. The approver confirms it, or asks for option 3 before a production caller uses `getAdvisor`; then a change record is needed if the package text changes.
+- `pnpm arch` keeps the port inside `integration`; the tests in `erp-fake`, `integration`, `identity` and `apps/worker` cover the read.
