+# draft-advisor-master-data: Read advisor master data from the ERP
+
+- **Jira:** none yet. A person creates the story; then this folder moves to `docs/specs/AN-<n>/`
+- **Gate:** design (trigger 2: new ERP port operation and payload contract)
+- **Status:** Draft
+- **Approved-by:**
+- **Baseline:** Discovery v0.1
+- **Module:** identity. Touches: integration (public API, new read `readAdvisor`), erp-port (new operation), erp-fake (seed advisor), apps/worker (wiring)
+
+## Context
+
+Head office needs the advisor master data that the ERP holds (T2-C-010). The platform has only the customer read. Direct request; ADR: [ADR-0017](../../adr/0017-erp-advisor-master-data-read.md).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+No AC ID in the register covers this read yet. The tests start their titles with the requirement ID T2-C-010.
+
+| Requirement | Test |
+|---|---|
+| T2-C-010 | `packages/erp-fake/src/erp-fake.test.ts`, `packages/core/src/integration/integration.test.ts`, `packages/core/src/identity/identity.test.ts`, `apps/worker/src/worker.test.ts` |
+
+Behaviour asked for in the request:
+
+1. `identity.getAdvisor(advisorNumber)` returns `{ advisorNumber, givenName, familyName, email, active, sourceVersion, readAt }` for an advisor that exists in the ERP.
+2. It returns `null` when the ERP has no such advisor.
+3. The fake ERP has advisor `B20001`.
+4. `createApp()` in `apps/worker` exposes it as `app.identity.getAdvisor`.
+
+## Design increment
+
+- **Module file:** `identity/AGENTS.md`: `createIdentity({ repo, bus, integration, clock })`, `.getAdvisor(advisorNumber)`, type `Advisor`, invariant "advisor master data is read on demand and not stored". `integration/AGENTS.md`: `Integration.readAdvisor(advisorNumber)`. `erp-port/AGENTS.md`: `AdvisorMasterData`. `erp-fake/AGENTS.md`: `fakeAdvisors`.
+- **Contracts:** ERP port operation `readAdvisor(advisorNumber): AdvisorMasterData | null`. Payload `AdvisorMasterData`: `advisorNumber` (`B` + 5 digits), `givenName`, `familyName`, `email`, `active` (boolean), `sourceVersion`. No events.
+- **Schema:** none. The advisor data is not stored.
+
+## Local decisions
+
+- `getAdvisor` reads the ERP on each call, without a copy: the request asks for the ERP data, and a copy needs a table and a schedule that no story asks for yet.
+- `getAdvisor` returns a flat object; `sourceVersion` and `readAt` come from the `ErpRead` envelope. `source` is dropped because it is always `erp`.
+- An ERP outage throws `ErpUnavailableError` to the caller; the request names no fallback. `integration` re-exports the error so callers can catch it without importing the port.
+- `createIntegration` wraps both reads with one helper that builds the `ErpRead` envelope; `readCustomer` behaves as before.
+- `identity` takes `integration` as a required dependency; `identity` tests use a stub of the `Integration` interface, because only `integration` tests may load `erp-fake`.
+- Seed advisor `B20001` is "Berta Beraterin", `berta.beraterin@example.test`, active, source version `v2`. It is the advisor of seed customer `K100001`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- A read copy of advisors in `erp_copy`, its schedule and reconciliation.
+- Authorisation of head office staff for this read, and a head office screen.
+- The NAV adapter mapping of the payload.
+
+## Open questions
+
+- Which AC ID covers this read? The register has only the flow T2-C-010. The tests use T2-C-010 until an AC ID exists, so `pnpm trace` does not count them.
+- Live read or copy? T2 section 4 allows synchronous ERP reads only at the checkout, and T3-D-007 fills copies by schedule or event. This spec reads live, as the request asks. If the approver wants a copy instead, the story adds an `erp_copy` table and a schedule (trigger 3); if the live read stays, Provital may need a change record (trigger 5).
+- Does head office need a fallback (last copy) when the ERP is down?
+
+## Deviations
+
+None.
